It is already March, but the weather in Berlin is still very cold.
I walk to the U-Bahn in the morning.
An icy wind is blowing through the streets today.
I am walking fast, because I am freezing.
In the morning I always put on a thick sweater.
Over that I then wear my thin jacket from Mexico.
The thick sweater is cozy, but that is not enough today.
The cold air goes right through the thin jacket.
My hands and my face are freezing cold.
This cold weather is still new to me.
The Mexican jacket is very beautiful, but it is useless here.
I need a long coat or a really thick jacket.
A warm winter coat is absolutely important for Berlin.
I do not want to freeze on the way to work anymore.
A good coat is often expensive, but I am buying one.
I will look for a good shop for clothes this evening.
